WEBVTT

1

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.250

Four years we wasted squabbling

over a peninsula's sovereignty.



2

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:28.542

And our two main battle Titans were

nearly shredded by the enemy fleet.



3

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:34.458

"Human ingenuity surpasses

and shatters Marley's Armor at last."



4

00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:39.958

The press from other nations

is commending the Mid-East Forces.



5

00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:44.000

Does this sound like a victory

for Marley to you?



6

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.042

Magath, do you care to comment?



7

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:50.625

General, I'm afraid the time has come.



8

00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:55.042

That is, humanity has eclipsed

the Power of the Titans.



9

00:00:55.042 --> 00:01:00.333

While we've been relying heavily

on Titans and colonial expansion,



10

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:04.917

other nations have been developing

weapons to counter us.



11

00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:09.542

As a result, our strategy has

come back to bite us on the ass.



12

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:15.792

For the time being, our Titans remain

unrivaled when it comes to land battles.



13

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:22.542

However, if aircraft keep advancing at

this rate, bombs will soon fall like rain.



14

00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:29.708

All while Titans, the devils of the earth,

can do nothing but look up and watch.



15

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:37.583

Do we not have any Titans with wings?



16

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:40.833

General, I'm trying to say

that the era of Titans--



17

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.417

I know.



18

00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:46.458

In the near future,

we will lose our initiative in war.



19

00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:49.375

No, perhaps we already have.



20

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:56.333

Though once the heroes who crushed

the Eldian devils, look at what we've become.



21

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.875

If I may, General?



22

00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:01.833

Requesting permission to give counsel.



23

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:06.250

Zeke, the wonderboy. Go ahead.



24

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:12.250

We should resume the Paradis Island Operation

and recover the Founding Titan.



25

00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:20.208

As Commander Magath was saying,

Marley needs to develop better weapons.



26

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:25.167

However, the world will not stand by and wait.



27

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:29.125

Our military needs time

to completely restructure.



28

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:33.167

But for that, the newspapers

of the world must read this:



29

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:38.542

"Marley Occupies Paradis

and Wields the Power of All Titans."



30

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:44.375

You have one year left

in your term, correct?



31

00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:50.958

Yes, and I'm concerned that Colt can't

inherit the full power of the Beast Titan.



32

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:54.292

I see.



33

00:02:54.292 --> 00:03:00.167

In your last year, you wish to redeem

yourself for your defeat four years ago?



34

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.333

That is correct.



35

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:07.417

The sick exploits of Grisha Jaeger

should be brought to an end



36

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:11.417

by none other than me, his former son.



37

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:45.958

"Midnight Train"



38

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.750

Sorry I bashed you to further my agenda, Colt.



39

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.750

Don't be. You were amazing.



40

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.667

To think, an Eldian being heard by the general!



41

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:07.417

There hasn't been a Beast

like you in its history.



42

00:05:07.417 --> 00:05:11.375

Sometimes it reminds me

of the Founding Titan.



43

00:05:11.375 --> 00:05:16.708

Why are you so special?

It's not like you have any royal blood.



44

00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:21.417

Who knows? Guess I'll be dead

before we figure it out.



45

00:05:21.417 --> 00:05:27.708

Oh... But when you inherit my memories,

you'll find out my big secret.



46

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:30.000

Secret? What is it?



47

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.792

The special way I wipe my ass.

Hope you don't tell anyone.



48

00:05:34.792 --> 00:05:36.792

Too late. I want a report.



49

00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:38.042

--Commander!

--Commander!



50

00:05:38.042 --> 00:05:43.500

Everything down to the hairs on your ass.

Do you think Eldians get privacy?



51

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.458

No, sir!



52

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.833

You can conquer Paradis in a year?



53

00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:56.250

It's more like I only have

one year left to try.



54

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:02.083

These past three years, every scout ship

we've sent to Paradis hasn't returned.



55

00:06:02.083 --> 00:06:05.208

Zeke, what do you think of that?



56

00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:12.125

Considering 32 ships were sunk, I can't

imagine a single Titan was responsible.



57

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:19.000

At least two Titans, including Eren Jaeger,

must have blocked their escape.



58

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.292

I agree. If we attack the island,

our ships will need support.



59

00:06:24.292 --> 00:06:29.792

Yes. But it's more than their Titans

that pose a threat.



60

00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:36.375

Wai--



61

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:46.250

It seemed like you were having a

good dream, so I didn't wake you.



62

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:51.417

I still haven't thanked you

for back then. Galliard...



63

00:06:51.417 --> 00:06:53.083

Thank you.



64

00:06:53.083 --> 00:06:55.292

Don't thank me.



65

00:06:55.292 --> 00:07:01.917

If I inherited the Armored Titan nine

years ago, this wouldn't have happened.



66

00:07:01.917 --> 00:07:07.167

My brother wouldn't have protected you

and been eaten by a Titan, either.



67

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.167

You saw Marcel's memories?



68

00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:15.417

No, but I learned enough from

that girl before me, Ymir.



69

00:07:15.417 --> 00:07:19.750

What an impressive name

for such a pitiful woman.



70

00:07:21.042 --> 00:07:25.167

Isn't it thanks to her that we

got my brother's Jaw back?



71

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:27.750

Yeah, that's right.



72

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:31.125

What the hell were you doing on that island?



73

00:07:31.125 --> 00:07:34.042

Getting saved by someone new every day?



74

00:07:34.042 --> 00:07:34.917

Yeah.



75

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.958

I saw how you acted through her memories.



76

00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:43.042

What's with that?

Pretending to be a reliable guy, huh?



77

00:07:43.042 --> 00:07:45.583

I'd say you were imitating my brother!



78

00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:50.250

Pock, let's not pick on people

who just took cannons to the face.



79

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.042

Quit calling me that, Pieck.



80

00:07:53.042 --> 00:07:54.250

You all right?



81

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.375

It's been two months

since I've been a human.



82

00:07:57.375 --> 00:08:00.958

I kinda forgot the whole bipedal thing.



83

00:08:00.958 --> 00:08:04.833

By the way, Reiner...

You oughta see Gabi and the others.



84

00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:07.083

They're worried about you.



85

00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:08.875

Think I will.



86

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.208

I'm pooped.



87

00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:18.833

Feels like ages since I've seen you.



88

00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:22.958

Really? Even though we're

always fighting together?



89

00:08:22.958 --> 00:08:26.250

Well, we might not have to for a while.



90

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.167

Let's hope so.



91

00:08:31.417 --> 00:08:33.500

--This way.

--Sure.



92

00:08:34.792 --> 00:08:39.083

Hey, if Titans lose their usefulness in battle,



93

00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:43.708

what will happen to the

Warrior unit and us Eldians?



94

00:08:45.792 --> 00:08:46.958

--A guy that lives near me said

the sea is so salty 'cuz he pisses in it.



95

00:08:46.958 --> 00:08:49.125

--Mr. Braun will be fine.

--A guy that lives near me said

the sea is so salty 'cuz he pisses in it.



96

00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:50.708

--I know.

--A guy that lives near me said

the sea is so salty 'cuz he pisses in it.



97

00:08:50.708 --> 00:08:53.458

--Huh? That's...

--A guy that lives near me said

the sea is so salty 'cuz he pisses in it.



98

00:08:55.667 --> 00:09:00.667

They're probably enemy soldiers

that survived the Pure Titan attack.



99

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:05.375

Once they get home, they'll talk about

how inhumane Titan warfare is!



100

00:09:05.375 --> 00:09:09.292

It'll just make things

even worse for us Eldians!



101

00:09:09.292 --> 00:09:13.333

"People of the world!

Let us kill the Subjects of Ymir!"



102

00:09:15.375 --> 00:09:17.583

--Shit! Shit! Shit! Shit!



103

00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:20.167

--Cut it out, Udo.

--Shit! Shit! Shit! Shit!



104

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:22.542

Don't beat up the city.



105

00:09:22.542 --> 00:09:24.417

Reiner!



106

00:09:24.417 --> 00:09:26.208

You're okay to walk?!



107

00:09:26.208 --> 00:09:29.292

Yeah. Are you guys all right?



108

00:09:29.292 --> 00:09:31.083

--Gabi.

--Yup!



109

00:09:31.083 --> 00:09:33.292

--Udo.

--I guess.



110

00:09:33.292 --> 00:09:36.500

--Zofia.

--Same old.



111

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.292

Falco.



112

00:09:38.292 --> 00:09:39.083

Hello.



113

00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:43.083

Hey! They said we're going back to Liberio!



114

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:44.917

Let's walk around till then!



115

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:45.875

Hey!



116

00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:47.083

We never get chances like this!



117

00:09:47.083 --> 00:09:50.458

Shouldn't Mr. Braun be resting?



118

00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:55.625

I'm all right. Don't worry.



119

00:09:55.625 --> 00:09:57.708

<i>You </i>go home and rest!



120

00:09:57.708 --> 00:09:59.542

I'm coming, too!



121

00:09:59.542 --> 00:10:03.292

Hold up, Gabi. Commander Magath

said that's not a place kids--



122

00:10:03.292 --> 00:10:06.542

But I just saw him walking that way.



123

00:10:07.958 --> 00:10:10.000

You worrywart.



124

00:10:15.125 --> 00:10:16.083

Wait!



125

00:10:16.083 --> 00:10:17.250

Huh?



126

00:10:22.167 --> 00:10:24.708

You kids are too young for that store.



127

00:10:24.708 --> 00:10:26.917

Aww!



128

00:10:30.875 --> 00:10:35.792

Did you guys witness the bravery

of our Eldian goddess?!



129

00:10:35.792 --> 00:10:40.667

Gabi took on the armored train

in place of 800 Eldian soldiers!



130

00:10:40.667 --> 00:10:43.083

Man, Colt! You stink of booze!



131

00:10:43.083 --> 00:10:46.375

Why'd you do it, you big idiot?!



132

00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:52.250

Comrades! Do you have any idea

why this idiot risked her life?!



133

00:10:52.250 --> 00:11:00.042

Well, I do! She did it to save

all your asses in the Eldian unit!



134

00:11:00.042 --> 00:11:03.458

Yeah!



135

00:11:03.458 --> 00:11:05.875

I'll go shut 'em up.



136

00:11:05.875 --> 00:11:07.750

Let 'em have it.



137

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.083

Just this one night.



138

00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:16.375

--Gabi! Gabi! Gabi...!

--Me! Me! Me...!



139

00:11:16.375 --> 00:11:18.958

They're lifting her up again.



140

00:11:18.958 --> 00:11:21.792

They shouldn't let my brother drink.



141

00:11:21.792 --> 00:11:24.833

And Gabi gets carried away too easily.



142

00:11:24.833 --> 00:11:30.708

Still, it's looking like she'll be the one

who inherits the Armored Titan.



143

00:11:30.708 --> 00:11:35.792

Yeah. The girl who adores you

will inherit your Titan...



144

00:11:35.792 --> 00:11:38.542

...and will live till she's 27.



145

00:11:39.458 --> 00:11:43.500

If cannons don't shred her first, that is.



146

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.875

Are you fine with that?



147

00:11:47.417 --> 00:11:53.917

What did you say? Are you insulting

the honor of inheriting one of the Nine?



148

00:11:53.917 --> 00:11:59.292

If I report this, you and your whole

family will become Titan weapons.



149

00:11:59.292 --> 00:12:03.583

W-Wait! Let me rephrase what I said!



150

00:12:03.583 --> 00:12:09.167

I, Falco Grice, hope to be freed from

the evil blood of Ymir and my ancestors!



151

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:11.417

I pledge my life to Marley!



152

00:12:11.417 --> 00:12:15.458

And what about the honor

of inheriting one of the Nine?



153

00:12:15.458 --> 00:12:18.500

I would be proud to be an Honorary Marleyan



154

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:23.208

and be given the chance to display

my loyalty to our motherland!



155

00:12:23.208 --> 00:12:26.250

Do you want to inherit the Armored?



156

00:12:28.583 --> 00:12:31.667

Thank you!



157

00:12:31.667 --> 00:12:34.500

The one who should inherit it... is me!



158

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:35.458

Yes.



159

00:12:35.458 --> 00:12:37.333

Huh?



160

00:12:37.333 --> 00:12:42.917

You have to rescue Gabi from

the dark future that awaits us.



161

00:12:44.958 --> 00:12:49.958

"Armbands are used to differentiate the Eldian

'devils.' It is mandatory for Eldians in Marley

to wear their armband when they go outside.

Failure to do so will result in punishment."



162

00:13:01.208 --> 00:13:03.333

We're back!



163

00:13:03.333 --> 00:13:05.625

We made it back alive!



164

00:13:05.625 --> 00:13:08.833

It's our beloved hometown, Liberio!



165

00:13:08.833 --> 00:13:10.292

--We're home!



166

00:13:10.292 --> 00:13:11.708

--Gabi...

--We're home!



167

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:14.167

Could you please tone it down?



168

00:13:14.167 --> 00:13:15.792

Ow, ow...



169

00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:20.375

You should've known

you can't hold your booze.



170

00:13:20.375 --> 00:13:23.458

Who's the one who gave him the drinks?



171

00:13:23.458 --> 00:13:25.917

He looked like he wanted some.



172

00:13:25.917 --> 00:13:31.083

Unbelievable. How dare you spew

Pieck's kindness all over the train.



173

00:13:31.083 --> 00:13:34.125

We should've shut 'em up last night.



174

00:13:35.167 --> 00:13:37.833

I heard they kept hoisting you up.



175

00:13:37.833 --> 00:13:39.375

Because of Colt!



176

00:13:39.375 --> 00:13:45.750

I think it's fine. You deserved a bit of fun.

What you did was impressive.



177

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.625

Pieck!



178

00:13:49.792 --> 00:13:52.542

Vice Chief Braun...



179

00:13:52.542 --> 00:13:59.125

What if he's thinking the same as me...

and he wants us Eldians to be free from war?



180

00:14:00.125 --> 00:14:03.417

Can I... trust him?



181

00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:14.625

Later. Take it easy and enjoy the break.



182

00:14:14.625 --> 00:14:17.542

Not me! It's back to training tomorrow!



183

00:14:17.542 --> 00:14:21.083

Trying to boost your grades? Gimme a break.



184

00:14:21.083 --> 00:14:22.625

I am not!



185

00:14:22.625 --> 00:14:26.875

Hey, you two. Don't push yourselves too hard.



186

00:14:38.125 --> 00:14:39.625

Dad!



187

00:14:43.833 --> 00:14:45.083

Zeke...



188

00:14:45.083 --> 00:14:47.833

Grandpa! Grandma!



189

00:14:47.833 --> 00:14:49.750

I'm home!



190

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.292

You achieved great things, Zeke.



191

00:14:52.292 --> 00:14:54.500

No, not yet.



192

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.250

Colt! Falco!



193

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.958

Colt!



194

00:14:57.958 --> 00:15:00.417

Dad! Mom!



195

00:15:00.417 --> 00:15:02.542

--Gabi!

--Gabi!



196

00:15:05.292 --> 00:15:06.792

Reiner.



197

00:15:07.792 --> 00:15:11.542

You must be tired. Come home and rest.



198

00:15:11.542 --> 00:15:15.625

Mom... I think I will.



199

00:15:18.292 --> 00:15:19.625

Go on ahead!



200

00:15:19.625 --> 00:15:24.250

For crying out loud!

Do you not know how to stand?



201

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.625

Are they injured soldiers, Mr. Koslow?



202

00:15:26.625 --> 00:15:29.708

Huh? Stay outta the way, brat.



203

00:15:29.708 --> 00:15:32.708

They're Eldians with emotional trauma.



204

00:15:32.708 --> 00:15:34.292

Even our guys?!



205

00:15:34.292 --> 00:15:38.083

It's from digging trenches

on the front lines too long.



206

00:15:38.083 --> 00:15:41.458

All those bullets and bombs do it to you.



207

00:15:43.375 --> 00:15:45.000

Boom!



208

00:15:46.583 --> 00:15:49.250

Look! They fell over again!



209

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.500

You okay? It's all right!



210

00:15:53.583 --> 00:15:56.167

Your armband's on the wrong arm.



211

00:15:56.167 --> 00:16:02.917

It's okay. I'm sure you'll get better.

You don't have to fight anymore.



212

00:16:02.917 --> 00:16:04.333

Boom!



213

00:16:04.333 --> 00:16:05.667

Whoa!



214

00:16:05.667 --> 00:16:09.792

Just like I planned, I blew the

armored train right off the tracks!



215

00:16:09.792 --> 00:16:14.792

It actually worked! But as I ran away,

they fired a machine gun at me!



216

00:16:14.792 --> 00:16:17.375

And just before I ate lead...



217

00:16:17.375 --> 00:16:21.000

...Galliard protected me with the Jaw Titan!



218

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.750

Amazing, Gabi!



219

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:29.458

You and your bravery saved a bunch

of our soldiers! You're the savior of Eldia!



220

00:16:29.458 --> 00:16:32.000

I'm so proud of you!



221

00:16:33.083 --> 00:16:37.375

Reiner. Do you think Gabi

will become a Warrior?



222

00:16:37.375 --> 00:16:42.750

Yeah. It's almost a given she'll

inherit the Armored Titan.



223

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.708

That's good to hear.



224

00:16:44.708 --> 00:16:49.667

To think our family would have

two Warriors. I'm so proud.



225

00:16:49.667 --> 00:16:57.625

If only those island devils disappeared,

we Eldians could finally be happy.



226

00:16:57.625 --> 00:17:03.167

But, Reiner... Even you barely escaped

from the island devils, right?



227

00:17:03.167 --> 00:17:05.125

Don't, Dad!



228

00:17:05.125 --> 00:17:09.875

He survived on that island

of rotten devils for five years!



229

00:17:09.875 --> 00:17:15.042

Even if it wasn't classified,

it's stuff he wouldn't wanna talk about.



230

00:17:15.042 --> 00:17:19.208

You're right. Forgive me, nephew.



231

00:17:19.208 --> 00:17:22.667

No, I can talk about it.



232

00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:25.792

I infiltrated their military.



233

00:17:25.792 --> 00:17:30.833

Every last one of 'em

was a savage, heartless devil.



234

00:17:30.833 --> 00:17:35.042

During the entrance ceremony,

one of them started eating a potato.



235

00:17:35.042 --> 00:17:39.042

The instructor yelled at them,

but they hardly seemed to care.



236

00:17:39.042 --> 00:17:41.875

Said they stole it 'cuz it looked tasty.



237

00:17:41.875 --> 00:17:47.917

Realizing they crossed the line,

they said they'd share half with him.



238

00:17:47.917 --> 00:17:52.875

But the piece of potato they offered

wasn't even close to half.



239

00:17:52.875 --> 00:17:56.250

Being considerate doesn't

even cross their minds.



240

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:59.542

They're truly beyond all help.



241

00:17:59.542 --> 00:18:03.750

There was an idiot who forgot

why he went to the bathroom...



242

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:07.042

An insincere jerk who only

thought about himself...



243

00:18:07.042 --> 00:18:10.375

An uptight oaf who only

cared what others thought...



244

00:18:10.375 --> 00:18:15.917

A single-minded fool who charged ahead

and the chumps who followed him...



245

00:18:15.917 --> 00:18:18.500

There were all sorts of people there.



246

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.792

And we were there, too.



247

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.125

My days there were true hell.



248

00:18:30.917 --> 00:18:34.708

I've said too much. Forget it.



249

00:18:34.708 --> 00:18:39.667

What do you mean, "all sorts of people"?

They're bad people, right?



250

00:18:39.667 --> 00:18:45.000

That's right, Gabi. Those island devils

turned our world into hell.



251

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:50.333

There's no knowing when they'll attack

with giant Titans and flatten the world.



252

00:18:50.333 --> 00:18:55.333

It's up to good Eldians like us

to make sure they never do.



253

00:18:55.333 --> 00:18:56.417

Mmm.



254

00:18:56.417 --> 00:19:02.375

Those who left us and fled to the

island deserved to be punished.



255

00:19:02.375 --> 00:19:05.292

They're the ones who abandoned us.



256

00:19:13.042 --> 00:19:16.625

What's wrong, Gabi? You seem down.



257

00:19:16.625 --> 00:19:19.333

Aunt Karina's worried about you.



258

00:19:19.333 --> 00:19:24.583

She says you changed after

coming back from the island alone.



259

00:19:24.583 --> 00:19:30.458

Her 12-year-old son came back a grown man.

You can't really blame her.



260

00:19:30.458 --> 00:19:32.750

It feels like you're lying.



261

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.375

Lying? About what?



262

00:19:35.375 --> 00:19:40.458

I don't know, but I think Aunt Karina does.



263

00:19:40.458 --> 00:19:41.708

I heard it was a soldier.



264

00:19:41.708 --> 00:19:44.042

That's awful.



265

00:19:45.583 --> 00:19:47.333

Good morning.



266

00:19:47.333 --> 00:19:49.167

Everyone's here?



267

00:19:49.167 --> 00:19:53.708

It's not every day we meet

in the war chief's room.



268

00:19:53.708 --> 00:19:55.417

Where's the brass?



269

00:19:55.417 --> 00:19:59.625

Not in this room.

Can't we just meet for some tea?



270

00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:01.333

Right...



271

00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:03.833

Now then,



272

00:20:03.833 --> 00:20:10.667

the last battle made it clear that normal

weapons will overtake Titans in the near future.



273

00:20:10.667 --> 00:20:15.833

The weaker Marley becomes,

the more the Eldian race is threatened.



274

00:20:15.833 --> 00:20:18.375

Our existence is in danger.



275

00:20:18.375 --> 00:20:25.458

To rectify this, Marley must obtain the

Founding Titan and Paradis' resources.



276

00:20:25.458 --> 00:20:30.750

The world must be strongly reminded

of the threat that island poses.



277

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:34.375

To tell that story, we need a narrator.



278

00:20:34.375 --> 00:20:37.708

The Tybur family will fulfill that role.



279

00:20:37.708 --> 00:20:40.708

The family holding the War Hammer Titan?



280

00:20:40.708 --> 00:20:46.042

It's said the Tyburs have never sent

the War Hammer Titan to enemy soil.



281

00:20:46.042 --> 00:20:52.333

They're influential abroad for driving away

King Fritz during the Great Titan War.



282

00:20:52.333 --> 00:20:54.958

The world will listen to them.



283

00:20:54.958 --> 00:20:57.917

That's Pieck for you! Precisely!



284

00:20:57.917 --> 00:21:02.417

But the Tyburs have been living

the life in their huge mansions.



285

00:21:02.417 --> 00:21:06.875

Why come out of the woodwork now

and pretend to be heroes?



286

00:21:06.875 --> 00:21:11.833

I know how you feel, but the Tyburs

are concerned about Marley, too.



287

00:21:11.833 --> 00:21:13.417

But we--



288

00:21:13.417 --> 00:21:17.083

If it saves our motherland

Marley, I'll be grateful.



289

00:21:17.083 --> 00:21:24.042

Our Warrior unit can cooperate with the Tyburs

and serve as the backbone for restoring Marley.



290

00:21:24.042 --> 00:21:28.583

Indeed. Here in Liberio,

there will be a festival soon.



291

00:21:28.583 --> 00:21:29.583

Festival?



292

00:21:29.583 --> 00:21:36.167

VIPs from abroad will be invited to hear

an announcement from the Tyburs:



293

00:21:36.167 --> 00:21:40.083

"Within a year, we'll control Paradis Island."



294

00:21:40.083 --> 00:21:45.917

The fate of Marley and all Eldians

rests in this plan. It cannot fail.



295

00:21:45.917 --> 00:21:51.833

For the future of our motherland Marley,

we must join our hearts as one.



296

00:21:51.833 --> 00:21:57.625

Galliard seems to have some complaints,

but he always gets the job done.



297

00:21:57.625 --> 00:22:00.750

If that's all they're saying, I'm not concerned.



298

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.542

Except that one line of Zeke's.



299

00:22:03.542 --> 00:22:05.167

Hmm?



300

00:22:05.167 --> 00:22:08.958

"Not in this room," huh?



301

00:22:19.042 --> 00:22:21.375

Am I going back...



302

00:22:22.375 --> 00:22:24.083

...to that island?



303

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:01.125

Honorary Marleyan. Esteemed Warrior.



304

00:24:01.125 --> 00:24:05.208

What he wanted to be. What he couldn't be.



305

00:24:05.208 --> 00:24:09.625

Is the path that he's walked down

truly the right one?



306

00:24:09.625 --> 00:24:12.096

Next episode: "The Door of Hope."

